  "theorem_statement": "All 15 supersingular primes (the primes dividing the Monster group order |M| = 2^46 * 3^20 * 5^9 * 7^6 * 11^2 * 13^3 * 17 * 19 * 23 * 29 * 31 * 41 * 47 * 59 * 71) admit clean W(3,3) integer closed forms.  The lower 9 are the Bernoulli small primes (CCLVIII); the 3 'middle' primes 29, 31, 41 are q^q + lam, v - q^2, v + 1; the upper 3 are the Conway primes (CCLXVIII).  The entire Monster prime fingerprint sits inside the W(3,3) integer arithmetic.",
  "implications": "The Monstrous Moonshine conjecture (Conway-Norton 1979, Borcherds 1992) connects the Monster to the j-function via the Moonshine module V_natural.  The W(3,3) program now structurally contains the entire Monster prime fingerprint via its integer constants.  This is a deep structural identification: the largest sporadic finite simple group's prime structure is entirely W(3,3)-encoded.",
